# nr-office-formula-lib-stats-distributions

## Registration: root-owned functions/mod.rs

Add (retain all existing declarations):

    mod jstat;
    mod distributions;

Append `distributions::FUNCTIONS,` to TABLES. jstat is a private kernel module,
not a second registry. No workspace/Cargo/dependency change is needed.

The installed namespace has 43 distinct distribution functions and 85 callable
export paths, including aliases' own properties (BINOMDIST.RANGE, CHIDIST.RT,
FDIST.RT, FINV.RT, TDIST.2T/RT, TINV.2T). The recorder enumerates function identities
and the actual export namespace. The twin requires every alias to resolve to its
canonical function pointer, not a fabricated compatibility wrapper.

## Reuse prerequisites: root-owned statistical.rs visibility only

Expose the already-implemented elementary reductions to sibling modules:

    fn jsum(array: &[f64]) -> f64
    -> pub(super) fn jsum(array: &[f64]) -> f64

    fn mean(array: &[f64]) -> f64
    -> pub(super) fn mean(array: &[f64]) -> f64

T.TEST uses that reverse-order jStat mean. Poisson CDF builds its increasing-k
terms, then uses that same reverse-order jsum. Do not replace either by AVERAGE,
whose installed implementation adds forward. If mixed-NaN replay exposes operand
selection in the shared jsum, fix it once using shared math::add, not a duplicate
sum kernel in this task. The new modules cannot typecheck before this visibility
change; this is an explicit prerequisite, not an implemented stub.

Other reuse: engineering::erf (the existing jStat Chebyshev polynomial),
engineering::int32, shared V8 math/radix and production registry COMBIN/SUM/
AVERAGE/STDEV.S. These are already in the task base. The local numeric carrier N
only routes +/* to shared V8 add/mul while retaining the source expression order;
all transcendental operations call mixdog-js. No platform-libm approximation or
second erf polynomial was introduced.

jStat.factorial/combination are deliberately distinct from formulajs FACT/COMBIN:
the former use gammafn/gammaln and the 170 threshold. BINOM.DIST.RANGE and
HYPGEOM.DIST call the actual formulajs COMBIN through the registry, whereas
jStat's binomial/negative-binomial PDF uses its gamma-based combination.
The installed HYPGEOM.DIST does not reach jStat.hypgeom; it has its own COMBIN
formula. Installed T.DIST dispatches 1/2 to one/two-tailed CDF, not a PDF. No
unreachable jStat sampling APIs or unrelated distribution kernels were added.

## Source-derived kernels

Original node_modules/jstat 1.9.6 dist/jstat.js:
- gammaln, gammafn, gammap/lowRegGamma, factorial/factorialln/combination,
  betafn/betaln/betacf, gammapinv, ibeta/ibetainv, erfcinv.
- beta, centralF, chi-square, exponential, gamma, lognormal, normal, student-t,
  binomial (including its separate uncapped betinc), negative binomial, Poisson.
Original formulajs 4.6.1 wrappers retain argument-count and typeof gates, error
ordering, truthy cumulative selection, T.INV.2T bounds-before-error, CHISQ.TEST's
own recurrence/rounding, PROB's sorted-index quirk and Z.TEST's nested reparsing.
ibeta's observable Bool(false) is retained by F.DIST; negbin.pdf's invalid-count
Bool(false) and BINOM.INV/PROB Undefined results are not coerced to numeric outputs.

## Separate fixture set: do not overwrite descriptive statistics

Recorder: benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-stats-distributions.mjs
Set: native/core/fixtures/office-stats-distributions/
Files: golden.json, MANIFEST.json, LICENSE.formulajs, LICENSE.jstat.
Original office-stats recorder/fixtures (3,226 descriptive cases) are untouched.
Root indexes this new set separately in native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, or
uses a combined inventory referencing BOTH sets. Never replace the earlier set.
The new per-set manifest records source SHA-256s, version, 85 export paths,
43 bodies, 6,044 returned-value/exception cases and golden/license byte hashes.

Executed reference command (original node_modules read-only):
node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-stats-distributions.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --write
Without --write the recorder prints JSON only. Every original call is under a
200ms VM bound; an unexpected timeout aborts recording instead of becoming an
expected numeric/error result. Types, strings, booleans, undefined, errors,
exceptions and f64 bits (including NaN/sign/payload) are compared exactly.
No ULP allowance or normalization is present.

Explicit nontermination evidence: BINOM.INV(+Infinity,0.3,0.8) exceeded a separate
50ms VM probe. It is metadata, never an unbounded Rust replay or an invented error.
Ten alias/parameter-domain omissions are explicitly listed for infinite upper
bounds in BINOM.INV, BINOM.DIST.RANGE, HYPGEOM/NEGBINOM/POISSON cumulative loops.
The implementation keeps the source loop conditions and original fixed limits:
betacf 100, ibetainv 10, gammapinv 12, erfcinv 2, and source-derived lowRegGamma
ITMAX including its JS ToInt32 semantics. No arbitrary production cap is added.
These potentially unbounded synchronous functions must remain inside the owned
ext-worker process/cancellation boundary described by the financial task, not a
daemon thread or an in-process unit test of known nonterminating input.

## Required root validation

No cargo/build/Rust test/application/commit/download was run. Rustfmt parsed the
source; original Node recording is not proof that the Rust twin passes.
After registration and reduction visibility changes:
- every_distribution_and_legacy_property_alias_is_registered
- every_distribution_result_equals_original_bits_types_and_errors
- twin_live_stats_distributions (ignored opt-in Node rerecord)
- existing descriptive, engineering, math and engine suites, then offline clippy.
Any numerical mismatch remains a blocker until diagnosed; none is waived here.

## Pending shared Utf16 integration

All numeric inputs use common parse_number/to_js_number/flatten coercions, not a
blanket raw-string refusal. This task base predates Value::Utf16. On integration:
- distributions.rs::row_length must recognize raw string code-unit length for
  CHISQ.TEST's first-row length comparison (use is_text/text_units).
- tests/twin_stats_distributions.rs::encode is exhaustive and needs a Utf16 arm;
  decoder should accept raw code-unit fixtures through Value::from_utf16.
- jstat.rs contains no Value string matches and passes only Number to engineering::erf.
No shared Value/coerce/math file was copied or edited by this task.
